        },
        {
          "insert": " The session service owns the edit queue and staged proposals; the kernel owns spawning. The FIFO bridges a launch's per-session tools to the per-spawn hook, the same seam as the prompt-kit and canvas harnesses. It pairs launches with spawns by order alone, so it holds only while launches are serialized. A multi-user host replaces it with keyed binding."
